      "message": "\u003e the override of `initBinder`, `start`, `stop`, and `cleanup` will have to be removed. \n\nYes, this will simplify a lot this class\n\n\u003e `mService.isAvailable()` will also not be available.\n\nYou can still have it as a private method (or field) \n\n\u003e `BluetoothScanManagerBinder` will also not implement from `IProfileServiceBinder`.\nPerfect as `IProfileServiceBinder` force you to implement `cleanup` and this currently is an empty method (and should stay like this)\n\n\u003e `TransitionalScanHelper` is expecting a boolean value from `isTestModeEnabled` which comes from ProfileService\n\nthe testModeEnabled is passed as a lambda, since you currently have no test mode support in the ScanManager, you can pass a lambda that return false always ?\n\nThe only unit test using that is `testDump_doesNotCrash` which seems it doesn\u0027t care what the test mode is as long at is doesn\u0027t crash...\nOther test are external ones (permissionUI test O_o / pairing_test) and doesn\u0027t seems to rely on our behavior neither (but I may be wrong here! )\n\n\u003e so I guess we\u0027ll also have to add a mContext to this class?\n\nHaving a Context looks good to me",
